An open box is made from a $16$ cm by $10$ cm sheet of card by cutting a square of side $x$ cm from each corner and folding up the sides.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (5.6,0) node[midway, below] {$16$ cm} -- (5.6,3.5) node[midway, right] {$10$ cm} -- (0,3.5) -- cycle;
\draw (0.7,0) -- (0.7,0.7) -- (0,0.7);
\draw (4.9,0) -- (4.9,0.7) -- (5.6,0.7);
\draw (0,2.8) -- (0.7,2.8) -- (0.7,3.5);
\draw (5.6,2.8) -- (4.9,2.8) -- (4.9,3.5);
\draw (0,2.8) -- (0,3.5) node[midway, left] {$x$ cm};
\draw[dashed] (0.7,0.7) -- (4.9,0.7) -- (4.9,2.8) -- (0.7,2.8) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which expression gives the volume $V$ cm$^{3}$ as a function of $x$?

A rectangle has one side of length $x$ cm along the base of a right-angled triangle of base $20$ cm and height $15$ cm, with its opposite corner on the hypotenuse.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (5.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0,4.125);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$20$ cm};
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (A) node[midway, left] {$15$ cm};
\coordinate (a) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (b) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (a) -- ($(a)+(b)-(A)$) -- (b);
\draw (0,2.475) -- (2.2,2.475) node[midway, above] {$x$ cm};
\draw (2.2,2.475) -- (2.2,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which expression gives the area $A$ cm$^{2}$ of the rectangle as a function of $x$?
